# HSHS World installation and environment variables

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you actually have.

```env
# Firebase (front-end public config is already in js/config.js, but keeping these here helps scripts if needed)
FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key
FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project.firebaseapp.com
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id

# Supabase
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key

# Cloudflare R2
R2_ENDPOINT_URL=https://<accountid>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_r2_access_key
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_r2_secret_key
R2_BUCKET_NAME=hshs-world-media
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://pub-...r2.dev

# Backblaze B2
B2_ENDPOINT_URL=https://s3.us-west-000.backblazeb2.com
B2_KEY_ID=your_b2_key_id
B2_APPLICATION_KEY=your_b2_application_key
B2_BUCKET_NAME=hshs-world-backup

# Media processing
FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg

# Output / reporting
REPORTS_DIR=./reports
DIST_CSS_DIR=./dist-css
OUTPUT_DIR=./artifacts
```

Do not put real secrets in the repo. Keep them only in `.env`.
